    "Structure is genuinely weak: silhouette ~0.14. These are a defensible, stable, interpretable segmentation of a continuum, not 3 naturally separated populations.",
    "Subscale reliabilities are modest (short facets on heterogeneous topics); reported, not hidden.",
    "The subscales come from an EFA on the same data used to cluster; the 70/30 holdout partially mitigates this, but no independent confirmatory sample exists.",
    "CGPA is self-reported and banded, and including it in the primary model costs it as a validation variable.",
    "Sample imbalance: 79% male, 64% in years 1-2, 14 departments; personas describe the dominant strata best.",
    "The lexicon is single-coded: no second coder, so no inter-rater reliability figure and theme prevalences are lower bounds.",
    "The free text is never a clustering input, which is what makes theme-cluster agreement genuine corroboration - but it means this project cannot say whether the text alone would reproduce the same personas.",
    "Self-report, cross-sectional, single-site: no causal claim is available."
  ]
